```
The original code had double curly braces `{{` and `}}`. This is because it's used in a `.format()` call in `Console.export_html`:

```python
 2236             rendered_code = render_code_format.format(
 2237                 code="".join(fragments),
 2238                 stylesheet=stylesheet,
 2239                 foreground=_theme.foreground_color.hex,
 2240                 background=_theme.background_color.hex,
 2241             )
```

If I use single curly braces in the template, `.format()` will try to interpolate them and fail if they are not provided in the arguments.

In my edit, I used:
```python
body {
    color: {foreground};
    background-color: {background};
}
```
`{foreground}` and `{background}` are provided in `.format()`. But the `body { ... }` curly braces are NOT provided. So they must be escaped as `{{` and `}}`.

I need to fix this.

